## Why This Is Asked
Tests mastery of live CNF config delivery under scale, using dynamic route management, traffic shaping, and robust rollback. It probes understanding of drift detection, observability integration, and safe rollout in multi-tenant environments.

## Key Concepts
- Zero-downtime rolling updates with canary deployments
- Dynamic configuration distribution and consistency
- Drift detection and automated rollback with observability

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-implementation snippet to illustrate traffic weight update
async function rollWithCanary(nextWeight) {
  await distributeConfig({ tenants: 'all', weight: nextWeight });
  await monitorErrors(60_000);
  if (riskTooHigh()) rollback();
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you detect hidden slippage in latency during canary?
- How would you handle tenants with non-uniform traffic patterns during ramp?

## Why This Is Asked
This tests resilience‑oriented CNF design for multi‑tenant traffic, focusing on per‑tenant state, timing windows, and safe recovery

## Key Concepts
- Per-tenant state tracking within a sidecar
- Rolling window counters and cooldown handling
- 503 responses during open state, then auto‑recover

## Code Example
```javascript
class Breaker {
  constructor() { this.map = new Map(); }
  allow(tenant) {
    const s = this.map.get(tenant) || {f:0, t:0, open:0};
    const now = Date.now();
    if (now < s.open) return false;
    if (now - s.t > 60000) { s.f = 0; s.t = now; }
    const ok = s.f < 5;
    if (!ok) s.open = now + 30000;
    this.map.set(tenant, s);
    return ok;
  }
  fail(tenant) {
    const s = this.map.get(tenant) || {f:0, t:Date.now(), open:0};
    s.f += 1; s.t = Date.now(); this.map.set(tenant, s);
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How to test the breaker under load? Probe metrics and simulate bursts
- How to persist breaker state across restarts? Serializable store
- How to tune thresholds for different tenants?

## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates a candidate's ability to design comprehensive runtime security controls for cloud-native network functions, focusing on continuous compliance verification and automated remediation beyond static image signing.

## Key Concepts
- Runtime attestation and drift detection
- SBOM-based compliance validation
- Tenant-isolated cryptographic identity
- Mutual TLS for secure communication
- Policy enforcement with OPA/Kyverno
- Automated rollback and recovery mechanisms

